        <table class="doc-table">
            <tr><th class="doc-th">Code / Name</th><th class="doc-th">PDF</th><th class="doc-th">3MF</th><th class="doc-th">Inv</th><th class="doc-th">Notes</th></tr>
            [% FOREACH row IN [
                 ['FEMALE-HINGE-L1','?','Y','Y','Doors 3MF (multiple exported variants fold to one)'],
                 ['FEMALE-HINGE-R1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['MALE-HINGE-L1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['MALE-HINGE-R1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['HINGE-LATCH-L1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['HINGE-LATCH-R1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['HANDLE','?','Y','Y','Door handle'],
                 ['WINDOW','?','Y','Y','Window_Shape'],
                 ['FRONT-LH','?','Y','Y','Dryer Extras'],
                 ['FRONT-RH','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['BACK-LH-DRAWER','?','Y','Y','Back LH Drawer variant'],
                 ['BACK-LH-HPV','?','Y','Y','Back LH HPV variant'],
                 ['BACK-RH-DRAWER','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['BACK-RH-HPV','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['DRYER-BASE','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['DRYER-CAP','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['DRYER-SUPPORT-LH','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['DRYER-SUPPORT-RH','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['FOOT','?','Y','Y','Wheel support foot'],
                 ['CASE-1','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['CASE-2','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['CERCHIO','?','Y','Y','Wheel half (matches WHEEL)'],
                 ['GOMMA','?','Y','Y','Tire (Wheel-Tire)'],
                 ['MAIN','?','Y','Y','Dryer main body'],
                 ['PIPE','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['HYDRA-BDX-BAR','?','Y','Y','Hydra Roller Bar BDX'],
                 ['HYDRA-BSX-BAR','?','Y','Y','Hydra Roller Bar BSX'],
                 ['HYDRA-FDX-BAR','?','Y','Y','Hydra Roller Bar FDX'],
                 ['HYDRA-FSX-BAR','?','Y','Y','Hydra Roller Bar FSX'],
                 ['PTFE-BAR','?','Y','Y','PTFE Tube Bar 1-2 / 3-4'],
                 ['ROLLER-BAR-D3','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['ROLLER-BAR-S2','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['NMBR1','?','Y','Y','Bearing mount NMBR1'],
                 ['NMBR2','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['NMBR3','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['NMBR4','?','Y','Y',''],
                 ['ROLLER','?','Y','Y','Hydra roller'],
                 ['WHEEL','?','Y','Y','Dryer wheel (WHEEL)'],
                 ['WHEEL-M','?','Y','Y','Motor wheel (WHEEL-M)'],
                 ['DESICCANT-BOX','?','Y','Y','HDry Lite desiccant box'],
                 ['DESICCANT-LIP','?','Y','Y',''],
               ] %]
            <tr>
                <td class="doc-td"><code>[% row.0 %]</code></td>
                <td class="doc-td [% row.1 == 'Y' ? 'ok' : row.1 == 'N' ? 'miss' : 'warn' %]">[% row.1 %]</td>
                <td class="doc-td [% row.2 == 'Y' ? 'ok' : row.2 == 'N' ? 'miss' : 'warn' %]">[% row.2 %]</td>
                <td class="doc-td [% row.3 == 'Y' ? 'ok' : row.3 == 'N' ? 'miss' : 'warn' %]">[% row.3 %]</td>
                <td class="doc-td">[% row.4 %]</td>
            </tr>
            [% END %]
        </table>

        <h3 class="doc-h3">C. Hardware &amp; fasteners (PDF counts vs inventory HW-* SKUs)</h3>
        <table class="doc-table">
            <tr><th class="doc-th">Item</th><th class="doc-th">PDF qty / module</th><th class="doc-th">Inventory SKU</th><th class="doc-th">Match</th></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Screw M4 &times; 14 mm</td><td class="doc-td">180</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-M4-14</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Screw M3 &times; 20 mm</td><td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-M3-20</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Bearing 608zz</td><td class="doc-td">16</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-608ZZ</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Magnet 8 &times; 2 mm</td><td class="doc-td">20</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-MAG-8X2</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Adhesive gasket 6 &times; 3 mm</td><td class="doc-td">6 m</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-GASKET-6X3</code> + <code>INT-HDRY-GSK150/1582/180/215/358/378</code></td><td class="doc-td warn">? (sheet + cut lengths)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Washers</td><td class="doc-td">listed</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-WASHER</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Bolt &amp; nut (wheels)</td><td class="doc-td">listed</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-BOLT-NUT</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Spacer 50</td><td class="doc-td">&mdash;</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-SPACER-50</code></td><td class="doc-td warn">? (not in PDF extract)</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Polydryer</td><td class="doc-td">&mdash;</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-POLYDRYER</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
            <tr><td class="doc-td">Wheel kit (assembly)</td><td class="doc-td">&mdash;</td><td class="doc-td"><code>HW-WHEEL-KIT</code></td><td class="doc-td ok">Y</td></tr>
        </table>

        <h3 class="doc-h3">D. The "group plates" complication (why 3MF part count &ne; inventory count)</h3>
        <p class="doc-body">OrcaSlicer 3MF files store geometry as <code>3D/Objects/object_NN.model</code> and the human-readable
        part name lives in <code>Metadata/*.json</code> (plate config) &mdash; <strong>not</strong> in the filename. A single
        <code>Metadata/plate_N.png</code> thumbnail shows a whole build plate of many parts. Consequences:</p>
        <ul class="doc-ul">
            <li><strong>One plate &ne; one part.</strong> Module_1.3mf has ~40 model objects across 18 plate thumbnails; the named objects resolve to ~35 distinct codes (B01&ndash;B04, BBL/BBR/BL/BLS/BR/BRS, FL/FLS/FR/FRS, SBL/SBR, Board, caps, T01&ndash;T04, etc.).</li>
            <li><strong>Duplicate exports.</strong> The same physical part is exported under several names (e.g. <code>Roller_Bar_S2 (1)</code>, <code>Roller_Bar_S2 (1) (1)</code>, <code>SBL02 (1)</code>). These collapse to one inventory SKU each.</li>
            <li><strong>Variant ambiguity.</strong> Doors 3MF contains both <code>FFL01_Sensor</code> and <code>FFL01_no_Sensor</code>, and <code>FFR01_Dryer_Panel</code> vs <code>FFR01_no_panel</code>. Only one variant should be the "real" inventory row; the other is a build option. This is an open question for the BOM.</li>
            <li><strong>Hinge pairs.</strong> Female/Male hinge L1+R1 each appear as multiple exported STLs (<code>__1___1_.stl</code> suffixes in <code>nfs/hdry_parts/023037</code>); geometry-matched to one row each. The traveler must not double-count them.</li>
            <li><strong>Wheel composition unclear.</strong> The manual and files suggest one wheel = 2 half-wheels (<code>Cerchio</code>/<code>Wheel</code>) + 1 tire (<code>Gomma</code>) + foot (<code>Foot</code>), but inventory lists <code>WHEEL</code>, <code>WHEEL-HALF</code>, <code>WHEEL-TIRE</code>, <code>WHEEL-FOOT</code>, <code>WHEEL-M</code> separately &mdash; confirm the intended BOM assembly.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="doc-h3">E. Unresolved / gaps</h3>
        <ul class="doc-ul">
            <li><span class="warn">Upgrade-2 ZIP inner 3MF</span> part names were not parsed this session (binary deflate). Re-run with a 3MF-unzip that reads <code>Metadata/project_settings.config</code> to confirm whether Upgrade 2 adds new codes or only remixes existing ones.</li>
            <li><span class="warn">SBR03</span> is in the PDF (x1) but not on any parsed plate &mdash; verify it is a real part or a manual typo for SBR02.</li>
            <li><span class="warn">REINFORCEMENT</span> (Reinforcement_small) appears on Module plates but has no obvious matching inventory SKU &mdash; confirm whether it is a sub-part of SBL/SBR or a standalone item.</li>
            <li><span class="warn">PDF printed-part list</span> was read from text extraction (codes + counts). The manual's per-page exploded diagrams were not OCR'd page-by-page; a few codes may be mis-attributed between Module 1 / Module 2. Cross-check against the plate previews in <code>/static/images/3d/hdry/parts/</code>.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="doc-h3">F. Net reconciliation</h3>
        <p class="doc-body">Inventory (114 HDRY/HW SKUs) is a <strong>superset</strong> of what the parsed 3MFs + PDF describe &mdash;
        i.e. nothing in the drawings is missing from inventory, but inventory carries extra assembly/sub-SKUs (WHEEL-HALF, WHEEL-TIRE,
        INT-HDRY-001-P3678x build variants, HW-WHEEL-KIT) that are <em>not</em> individual printed codes in the manual. The real risk
        is <strong>not missing items</strong> but <strong>mis-counting</strong> due to the group-plate duplicates and variant forks above.
        Fixing the traveler's hardcoded origin skew (see changelog) makes the traveler read <code>item_origin</code> truthfully so these
        rows classify correctly instead of being force-flagged as printed.</p>

        <p class="doc-body doc-muted">Generated 2026-09-11 from local file scan + live :4003 inventory read. Re-run the scan if source files change.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<style>
.doc-table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; margin: 1rem 0; }
.doc-th, .doc-td { border: 1px solid var(--border-color, #ccc); padding: 4px 8px; text-align: left; vertical-align: top; }
.doc-th { background: var(--th-bg, #f0f0f0); font-weight: bold; }
.ok { color: var(--success-color, #1a7f37); font-weight: bold; }
.miss { color: var(--danger-color, #c00); font-weight: bold; }
.warn { color: var(--warning-color, #b8860b); font-weight: bold; }
.doc-muted { color: var(--muted-color, #777); font-size: 0.9em; }
</style>
